We also need to set candidate_clearance_established (via establish_clearance_* actions). Those require candidate_loading_verified, candidate_compliance_certificate_linked, candidate_loading_container_linked, loading_container_leg_linked, and certain leg loaded flags (origin_leg_loaded or destination_leg_loaded etc). We have multiple clearance establishment actions: establish_clearance_nominal (requires not origin_leg_loaded and not destination_leg_loaded), establish_clearance_origin_loaded (requires origin_leg_loaded, not destination_leg_loaded), establish_clearance_destination_loaded (requires not origin_leg_loaded, destination_leg_loaded), establish_clearance_full_load (requires both origin_leg_loaded and destination_leg_loaded). Each also sets candidate_clearance_established and route_sequence_context_set (except nominal only sets clearance). Actually nominal sets only candidate_clearance_established; the others set both clearance and route_sequence_context_set.

